From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ellington Kirby <ellingtonkirby31@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] SCL fork: FBP_NO_BACKGROUND=1 omits the background
 activity

The state-recovery families need a traffic-free control condition, and
background traffic cannot be switched off from a route file.
BackgroundBehavior spawns its road actors in initialise() - before any
scenario trigger can fire - and BackgroundActivityParametrizer only caps
later additions rather than despawning. Worse, zeroing its counts feeds
_get_road_radius() (background_activity.py:298-306), collapsing the
speed-control radius to one spawn distance: measured on Town13, the same
ten vehicles remained but mean speed halved (16.43 -> 7.68 m/s), turning
moving traffic into crawling obstacles.

The flag is read at behaviour-tree construction so the activity is never
built. Default (unset or 0) is upstream behaviour. Both route_scenario
copies (leaderboard + scenario_runner) changed together.

Scoring-semantics change: campaigns run with and without this flag are
not comparable.
---
diff --git a/leaderboard/leaderboard/scenarios/route_scenario.py b/leaderboard/leaderboard/scenarios/route_scenario.py
index 96b2137..844bd01 100644
--- a/leaderboard/leaderboard/scenarios/route_scenario.py
+++ b/leaderboard/leaderboard/scenarios/route_scenario.py
@@ -401,7 +401,15 @@ class RouteScenario(BasicScenario):
         self.scenario_triggerer = scenario_triggerer
 
         # Add the Background Activity
-        behavior.add_child(BackgroundBehavior(self.ego_vehicles[0], self.route, name="BackgroundActivity"))
+        # SCL fork: FBP_NO_BACKGROUND=1 omits the background activity entirely.
+        # It cannot be switched off from a route file - BackgroundBehavior
+        # spawns its road actors in initialise(), before any scenario trigger
+        # fires, and BackgroundActivityParametrizer only caps later additions
+        # while its zeroed counts collapse the speed radius and leave the
+        # traffic crawling instead of gone. Traffic-free control condition
+        # only; campaigns across this flag are not comparable.
+        if os.environ.get('FBP_NO_BACKGROUND') != '1':
+            behavior.add_child(BackgroundBehavior(self.ego_vehicles[0], self.route, name="BackgroundActivity"))
 
         behavior.add_children(scenario_behaviors)
         return behavior
diff --git a/scenario_runner/srunner/scenarios/route_scenario.py b/scenario_runner/srunner/scenarios/route_scenario.py
index 204db22..6c86b26 100644
--- a/scenario_runner/srunner/scenarios/route_scenario.py
+++ b/scenario_runner/srunner/scenarios/route_scenario.py
@@ -284,7 +284,15 @@ class RouteScenario(BasicScenario):
         behavior.add_child(scenario_triggerer)  # Tick the ScenarioTriggerer before the scenarios
 
         # Add the Background Activity
-        behavior.add_child(BackgroundBehavior(self.ego_vehicles[0], self.route, name="BackgroundActivity"))
+        # SCL fork: FBP_NO_BACKGROUND=1 omits the background activity entirely.
+        # It cannot be switched off from a route file - BackgroundBehavior
+        # spawns its road actors in initialise(), before any scenario trigger
+        # fires, and BackgroundActivityParametrizer only caps later additions
+        # while its zeroed counts collapse the speed radius and leave the
+        # traffic crawling instead of gone. Traffic-free control condition
+        # only; campaigns across this flag are not comparable.
+        if os.environ.get('FBP_NO_BACKGROUND') != '1':
+            behavior.add_child(BackgroundBehavior(self.ego_vehicles[0], self.route, name="BackgroundActivity"))
 
         behavior.add_children(scenario_behaviors)
         return behavior
